   "install": {
    "title": "Getting Started",
    "html": "<p>🖥️ <a href=\"https://www.onlook.com/install\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Download the Desktop App</a> (Recommended) – The fastest way to get started with Onlook.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>macOS (Apple Silicon · Intel x64) → <a href=\"https://www.onlook.com/install\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Download</a></li>\n<li>Windows – Coming soon. Join the <a href=\"https://www.onlook.com/waitlist?os=windows\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Windows waitlist here</a> and be emailed when we have updates.</li>\n<li>Linux – No Linux artifact is published and we're still gauging demand for Linux. Join the <a href=\"https://www.onlook.com/waitlist?os=linux\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Linux waitlist here</a> and be emailed when we have updates.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>🧑‍💻 Build from source – <a href=\"https://github.com/onlook-dev/onlook/blob/main/SOURCE_BUILD.md\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">SOURCE_BUILD.md</a> covers building and running Onlook on a Mac. No Onlook account or cloud keys needed.</p>",
    "truncated": false,
    "chars": 686
   },
   "usage": {
    "title": "Usage data",
    "html": "<p>Onlook collects product usage analytics to help us improve the app. In the official download they are on by default; a build from source asks first. You can turn them off in Settings, or set <code>STUDIO_TELEMETRY=0</code> to run or build without them. See the <a href=\"https://www.onlook.com/privacy-policy\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">privacy policy</a> for details.</p>",
    "truncated": false,
    "chars": 322
   },
